WEBVTT

00:00:00.423 --> 00:00:02.708
Lolly was built in the middle of the

00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:05.637
biggest change in how media gets made

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:08.670
since the printing press, by people who

00:00:08.739 --> 00:00:11.219
are neither panicked about AI nor

00:00:11.297 --> 00:00:13.294
breathless about it.

00:00:14.066 --> 00:00:16.675
This page states the project's position

00:00:16.764 --> 00:00:19.648
plainly and pairs every claim with the

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:23.111
mechanism that enforces it, so you can

00:00:23.173 --> 00:00:25.719
verify rather than trust.

00:00:26.461 --> 00:00:29.422
"We're drinking like the tap will run dry

00:00:29.496 --> 00:00:30.919
any moment.

00:00:31.669 --> 00:00:34.964
It won't - today's AI is the worst it will

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:36.245
ever be.

00:00:36.998 --> 00:00:40.049
If we survive the flood, it won't be by

00:00:40.115 --> 00:00:42.457
hoarding what's in the rusty water tank

00:00:42.518 --> 00:00:45.395
down the hill, full of sediment.

00:00:46.155 --> 00:00:48.916
It will be by irrigating and reclaiming

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:52.394
our land for a prosperous future."

00:00:53.132 --> 00:00:56.557
- Andy Fitzsimon, Architect of Lolly

00:00:57.469 --> 00:01:00.723
To be precise about it, because this page

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:04.018
argues that precision matters: the image

00:01:04.068 --> 00:01:07.444
above is generated, not photographed.

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:11.174
No camera was pointed at that homestead,

00:01:11.234 --> 00:01:13.919
because there is no homestead.

00:01:14.682 --> 00:01:17.591
It was prompted from Andy's home state of

00:01:17.655 --> 00:01:21.200
Queensland, Australia, but it did not grow

00:01:21.241 --> 00:01:24.067
up there - it grew up in a datacenter in

00:01:24.126 --> 00:01:26.119
the United States.

00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:30.023
It is faithful to a place without being a

00:01:30.091 --> 00:01:33.389
record of one, and that distinction is the

00:01:33.478 --> 00:01:36.525
entire reason its Content Credentials say

00:01:36.615 --> 00:01:37.569
so.

00:01:38.352 --> 00:01:40.941
Here is what that looks like when you

00:01:41.016 --> 00:01:42.343
check it.

00:01:43.134 --> 00:01:46.183
Nine steps survive in the file: five

00:01:46.241 --> 00:01:49.222
recorded by Google as it generated and

00:01:49.302 --> 00:01:52.285
watermarked the image, then four recorded

00:01:52.345 --> 00:01:56.135
by Lolly as it opened, created, marked and

00:01:56.195 --> 00:01:59.145
converted the version on this page.

00:01:59.948 --> 00:02:03.049
Lolly did not generate anything, and its

00:02:03.116 --> 00:02:04.893
entry says so.

00:02:05.672 --> 00:02:08.993
Andy's metaphor for a flood is this: the

00:02:09.056 --> 00:02:11.875
scarcity posture toward AI - invest

00:02:11.958 --> 00:02:14.391
everything in the few, diminish yourself

00:02:14.452 --> 00:02:17.521
today, and worry later - is drinking

00:02:17.615 --> 00:02:20.445
spoiled tank water while the rain sets in

00:02:20.513 --> 00:02:23.148
and floodwater races across the plains

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:24.619
toward you.

00:02:25.393 --> 00:02:28.202
Generated content is about to be

00:02:28.256 --> 00:02:30.269
effectively infinite.

00:02:31.029 --> 00:02:33.774
When something becomes infinite, its value

00:02:33.834 --> 00:02:36.426
moves to whatever remains scarce around

00:02:36.490 --> 00:02:39.972
it: trust, provenance, brand coherence and

00:02:40.032 --> 00:02:41.670
human judgment.

00:02:42.484 --> 00:02:45.389
Lolly is not a bigger bucket for the

00:02:45.495 --> 00:02:46.617
flood.

00:02:47.365 --> 00:02:49.924
It is irrigation - channels that direct

00:02:49.984 --> 00:02:53.106
the water, and soil where things actually

00:02:53.168 --> 00:02:54.245
grow.

00:02:55.381 --> 00:02:58.176
The stance, in five commitments

00:02:59.119 --> 00:03:02.206
AI is welcome as input, never as

00:03:02.266 --> 00:03:04.019
impersonation.

00:03:04.786 --> 00:03:07.788
Agents are first-class users of Lolly:

00:03:07.849 --> 00:03:10.477
they run the same tools people do, through

00:03:10.532 --> 00:03:14.472
the MCP server and URL mode, inside

00:03:14.532 --> 00:03:17.194
exactly the same constraints.

00:03:17.949 --> 00:03:20.998
A tool that cannot emit an off-brand asset

00:03:21.086 --> 00:03:24.486
for a person cannot emit one for an agent

00:03:24.548 --> 00:03:27.461
either - the guard-rails do not care who

00:03:27.543 --> 00:03:29.595
is throwing the ball.

00:03:30.359 --> 00:03:33.062
What no agent gets to do is pass its

00:03:33.144 --> 00:03:36.270
output off as something it is not.

00:03:37.055 --> 00:03:39.793
AI declares itself.

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:43.847
When AI generated the pixels, the export

00:03:43.908 --> 00:03:47.054
says so: a machine-readable assertion in

00:03:47.099 --> 00:03:49.914
the file's Content Credentials and a

00:03:49.975 --> 00:03:53.292
visible GEN AI badge when anyone verifies

00:03:53.346 --> 00:03:54.245
it.

00:03:55.046 --> 00:03:58.303
Lolly also reads and surfaces the AI

00:03:58.365 --> 00:04:01.812
declarations of files made elsewhere, and

00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:05.250
flags when a SynthID watermark is likely

00:04:05.312 --> 00:04:08.352
present - reading the declaration, not the

00:04:08.438 --> 00:04:10.344
watermark itself.

00:04:11.117 --> 00:04:14.028
Audiences deserve to know how media was

00:04:14.089 --> 00:04:16.850
made - that sentence appears on our

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:19.885
Inclusive Design page as an ethical

00:04:19.946 --> 00:04:22.909
commitment, and this is the machinery

00:04:22.969 --> 00:04:24.469
behind it.

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:28.019
Provenance is default-on.

00:04:28.781 --> 00:04:31.467
Exports carry Content Credentials by

00:04:31.525 --> 00:04:34.644
default, not as a buried setting.

00:04:35.410 --> 00:04:38.814
The chain covers edits and ingredients, so

00:04:38.893 --> 00:04:41.794
a work's history travels with it.

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:45.796
You can verify this yourself on any file

00:04:45.866 --> 00:04:47.669
Lolly produces.

00:04:48.429 --> 00:04:51.168
People stay the authors.

00:04:51.933 --> 00:04:55.156
Every input is ultimately a decision,

00:04:55.227 --> 00:04:58.245
triggered somewhere by a person, no matter

00:04:58.318 --> 00:05:01.234
how many systems or left turns it took to

00:05:01.294 --> 00:05:02.520
get here.

00:05:03.293 --> 00:05:07.519
An agent can carry a decision a long way.

00:05:08.284 --> 00:05:11.093
It cannot originate one.

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:14.267
The words, the image, the palette, the

00:05:14.334 --> 00:05:17.225
call that needed judgment: tools scale

00:05:17.277 --> 00:05:20.469
that judgment, they do not replace it.

00:05:21.232 --> 00:05:24.507
The tedious parts are what get automated:

00:05:24.570 --> 00:05:27.090
the brand-checking, the re-exporting at

00:05:27.174 --> 00:05:30.120
every size, the hand-localising.

00:05:30.909 --> 00:05:34.093
What remains is the authorship.

00:05:34.867 --> 00:05:37.243
Channels, not buckets.

00:05:38.013 --> 00:05:40.769
Today's models are the floor, not the

00:05:40.878 --> 00:05:44.015
ceiling, so we refuse to build anything

00:05:44.076 --> 00:05:46.720
whose value depends on hoarding access to

00:05:46.781 --> 00:05:47.769
them.

00:05:48.547 --> 00:05:52.093
The engine is open source, renders on your

00:05:52.156 --> 00:05:54.944
own device and works offline.

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:59.060
There is no model moat, no usage meter, no

00:05:59.130 --> 00:06:01.542
scarcity business attached to the flood

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:02.770
itself.

00:06:03.539 --> 00:06:05.726
The durable investment is the

00:06:05.814 --> 00:06:08.889
infrastructure around the water - and that

00:06:08.961 --> 00:06:12.119
infrastructure is what we give away.

00:06:13.243 --> 00:06:15.972
Human decision is the point

00:06:16.952 --> 00:06:20.035
Let us be crystal clear about what sits

00:06:20.113 --> 00:06:22.944
underneath every commitment above.

00:06:23.705 --> 00:06:26.363
Individuals shape the earth and our

00:06:26.425 --> 00:06:27.644
history.

00:06:28.411 --> 00:06:31.590
Their choices, made one at a time, become

00:06:31.650 --> 00:06:34.619
the world the rest of us live in.

00:06:35.403 --> 00:06:37.944
Their actions make it.

00:06:38.715 --> 00:06:41.726
That is not sentiment, it is simply how

00:06:41.827 --> 00:06:44.194
anything has ever happened.

00:06:44.991 --> 00:06:48.505
So we empower human decision and we do not

00:06:48.567 --> 00:06:50.269
compromise it.

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:53.418
The right to choose.

00:06:54.204 --> 00:06:55.715
Agency.

00:06:56.509 --> 00:06:57.992
Autonomy.

00:06:58.767 --> 00:07:02.186
The ability to decide and to act, and for

00:07:02.232 --> 00:07:04.494
that act to be yours.

00:07:05.274 --> 00:07:09.318
Tools here scale what a person decided.

00:07:10.079 --> 00:07:12.930
They do not decide instead of them, and

00:07:12.961 --> 00:07:16.169
they never quietly stand in for them.

00:07:16.938 --> 00:07:20.343
Where a decision is carried by automation,

00:07:20.404 --> 00:07:23.230
the record still leads back to the person

00:07:23.286 --> 00:07:26.283
who triggered it, however many systems and

00:07:26.344 --> 00:07:29.520
left turns it passed through on the way.

00:07:30.291 --> 00:07:33.148
We honour that end to end, and we record

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:36.361
it: for history, for accountability, for

00:07:36.433 --> 00:07:38.670
trust, and for tomorrow.

00:07:39.803 --> 00:07:41.737
What this is not

00:07:42.726 --> 00:07:44.618
Not a ban.

00:07:45.395 --> 00:07:48.997
Tools may use AI where it serves the work,

00:07:49.066 --> 00:07:51.977
and agents are a supported audience - see

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:53.869
AI Agents.

00:07:54.681 --> 00:07:57.393
Not a purity claim.

00:07:58.191 --> 00:08:01.114
Lolly reads provenance broadly and writes

00:08:01.176 --> 00:08:04.842
it honestly; it does not pretend to detect

00:08:04.935 --> 00:08:08.244
every generated pixel on the internet.

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:11.543
Not a moral panic.

00:08:12.323 --> 00:08:15.344
The flood is not the enemy.

00:08:16.128 --> 00:08:19.044
Unattributed water is.

00:08:20.174 --> 00:08:22.780
How to hold us to it

00:08:23.758 --> 00:08:26.151
Every commitment above is enforced in the

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:30.345
open codebase, not in a policy PDF: the

00:08:30.417 --> 00:08:33.818
provenance path, the GEN AI labelling and

00:08:33.865 --> 00:08:36.555
the no-trackers guarantee all ship with

00:08:36.627 --> 00:08:39.865
tests, and the Verify It Yourself page

00:08:39.925 --> 00:08:41.984
walks you through checking the claims

00:08:42.037 --> 00:08:44.270
against a real export.

00:08:45.012 --> 00:08:47.636
If you find a place where the code and

00:08:47.674 --> 00:08:51.420
this page disagree, the code is the bug.
